================================================================================
📤 HOW TO SUBMIT TO GITHUB?
================================================================================

OPTION 1: Use the Helper Script (EASIEST)
------------------------------------------
1. Open terminal in project folder
2. Run: ./git_setup.sh
3. Follow the instructions it gives you
4. Create a GitHub repository online
5. Copy the repository URL
6. Run the commands it tells you


OPTION 2: Manual Method
------------------------
1. Open terminal in project folder

2. Initialize Git:
   git init

3. Configure Git (first time only):
   git config user.name "Your Name"
   git config user.email "your.email@example.com"

4. Add files:
   git add http_status_checker.sh text_replacer.sh sample_input.txt README.md

5. Commit:
   git commit -m "Add shell scripting tasks"

6. Go to GitHub.com and create a new repository

7. Copy the repository URL (looks like: https://github.com/username/repo-name.git)

8. Link your local folder to GitHub:
   git remote add origin <paste-your-url-here>

9. Push to GitHub:
   git branch -M main
   git push -u origin main

10. Take screenshots of:
    - Terminal showing script outputs
    - GitHub repository page

11. Submit the GitHub URL in your portal


================================================================================
❓ TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

Problem: "Permission denied" when running script
Solution: Make it executable
    chmod +x http_status_checker.sh
    chmod +x text_replacer.sh

Problem: "curl: command not found"
Solution: Install curl
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install curl -y

Problem: Script shows weird characters instead of colors
Solution: This is normal in some terminals, the script still works

Problem: "No such file or directory"
Solution: Make sure you're in the right folder
    cd /home/vickytricky/Documents/Devops-Guvi/shell-task4
    pwd  (this shows your current location)


